# Preserve user-written comments

When replacing or editing lines that include user-written comments, **keep those comments** unless the change makes them incorrect or misleading.

Prefer preserving user documentation even when it is more verbose than the agent would normally write (example values, `.shape` notes, expected outputs, rationale, etc.).

## ✅ Preserve

```python
# Before
result = compute_rates(spikes)  # e.g. shape (n_neurons, n_bins) ≈ (120, 50)
# After (refactor only)
result = compute_rates(spikes, bin_size=bin_size)  # e.g. shape (n_neurons, n_bins) ≈ (120, 50)
```

## ❌ Do not strip casually

```python
# Before
result = compute_rates(spikes)  # e.g. shape (n_neurons, n_bins) ≈ (120, 50)
# Bad — comment removed for brevity
result = compute_rates(spikes, bin_size=bin_size)
```

## When removal/update is allowed

- The comment is now **wrong** (update it to match the new code, or remove if no accurate short note remains)
- The user explicitly asks to remove or tighten comments
- The comment documents removed code and no longer applies

## Rules

- Prefer keep/update over delete when editing comment-bearing lines
- Do not drop comments solely because they are verbose, informal, or “obvious”
- When rewriting a block, carry forward nearby user comments that still apply
